Additional Practice


Find constants a and b such that \dfrac{1}{(2k-1)(2k+1)}=\dfrac{a}{2k-1}+\dfrac{b}{2k+1} for all k\in\mathbb{N}.
Hence evaluate \dfrac{1}{1\times3}+\dfrac{1}{3\times5}+\dfrac{1}{5\times7}+\dots+\dfrac{1}{19\times21}


Prove that \dfrac{1}{1\times4}+\dfrac{1}{4\times7}+\dfrac{1}{7\times10}+\dots+\dfrac{1}{(3n-2)(3n+1)}=\dfrac{n}{3n+1} for n\in\mathbb{N}


Find the value of \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{3}}+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}+\sqrt{4}}+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{4}+\sqrt{5}}+\dots+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{99}+\sqrt{100}}


Show that \dfrac{1}{k(k+2)}=\dfrac{1}{2}\bigg(\dfrac{1}{k}-\dfrac{1}{k+2}\bigg) for all k\in\mathbb{N}.
Hence evaluate \dfrac{1}{1\times3}+\dfrac{1}{2\times4}+\dfrac{1}{3\times5}+\dots+\dfrac{1}{50\times52}


Prove that \sum_{k=1}^{n}\dfrac{1}{(2k-1)(2k+1)}=\dfrac{n}{2n+1} for n\in\mathbb{N}


Find constants a and b such that \dfrac{k}{(k+1)(k+2)}=\dfrac{a}{k+1}+\dfrac{b}{k+2} for all k\in\mathbb{N}.
Hence find \sum_{k=1}^{n}\dfrac{k}{(k+1)(k+2)}


Evaluate \dfrac{1}{\sqrt{1}+\sqrt{3}}+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{3}+\sqrt{5}}+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{5}+\sqrt{7}}+\dots+\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{97}+\sqrt{99}}


Show that \sqrt{k+1}-\sqrt{k-1}=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{k+1}+\sqrt{k-1}} for all k\geqslant2.
Hence evaluate \dfrac{2}{\sqrt{2}+\sqrt{0}}+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{3}+\sqrt{1}}+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{4}+\sqrt{2}}+\dots+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt{101}+\sqrt{99}}
